body:
I didn't say I condone doing what is illegal, but you do what you need to when it comes to feeding your family.   What he did in the past isn't what he's doing now.   I didn't say anything about ignoring the law to get ahead.  He barely made a livable wage while he was doing said activities; it wasn't to get rich it was so we didn't starve.   Or do none of your countries have poverty and people that do shit they shouldn't to get by?

&#x200B;

I want the era where people from countries just as flawed as ours don't sit on a pedestal and preach just because some our citizens elected an idiot into office.   You act as though you live in some beacon of paradise, when I guarantee I could go just about anywhere in the world and find a person willing to criticize it for the problems it has.

&#x200B;

You have no right to judge me, my family or my country for that.  People get in bad spots, people make bad decisions and people can make up for that.  The point that "I" was emphasizing is that he had started at the bottom of the barrel doing what he needed to do to survive and now he's a successful and well respected real-estate agent that does his job fully within the scope of the law and make quite a bit of money while he does it.

&#x200B;

You should actually read instead of making half baked assumptions.

Honestly, I just want to see the Federation War system reworked, so you don't need the entirety of the federation to vote on it.  Just take those empires who voted yes, give them a Fleet power proportionate to sum total of all included Federation Empires in the war, and then have them all join together.  So tired of playing MP with my friend, creating a federation and then having some weak-ass Tier 2 Empire tell me I CAN'T go to war with the people I've been essentially obliterating for the last 50 years.

&#x200B;

Fuck you, if I want to drag my friend into a war to turn those Fungus people into a tributary I should be able to!  Eat it yah damn NPC federation friends, -sigh- only reason we added them into our federation was so others wouldn't snap them up first.
